60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"I'm concerned about the availability of trained hands for the projects. The Microbiome Atlas project might face challenges due to the loss of phenotyping technicians to industry. The Plant Drought Signaling research could be impacted by the secondment of senior modelling analysts abroad. The Protein Folding Dynamics study aligns well with the influx of applicants for modelling and code posts. The Regeneration in Amphibians investigation might face issues due to the increased animal-unit day rates and the need for live breeding colonies.

I'm also worried about the shrinking buying power of the award. The increased costs for animal work and the freeze on travel and bench-fee lines are significant. We need to consider these factors when evaluating the proposals.

Lastly, the success of catalogue-style awards is encouraging. The Microbiome Atlas project fits this category and has shown long-term value. The improved national repository deposit turnaround is also a positive development that can benefit the broader scientific community.

I look forward to discussing the candidates and making an informed decision based on the information we've gathered.","{""words"":175,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
